PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The deliberation remains split between Camp G (Colleagues 1, 5, 7, 9, 13, 14) and Camp H (Colleagues 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 10, 11, 12). 

Proponents of G argue that the forward biosynthetic path from 3-Hydroxypropionate [B] to PEP [F] is uniquely defined by $k_2 k_3 k_4 k_5$, and that feedback merely shifts steady-state gain rather than providing an algebraic alternative. Conversely, proponents of H highlight that the prompt explicitly defines inhibitory edges ($-|$) and emphasizes that $k_{19}$ is "extremely large." This creates a dominant closed-loop negative feedback mechanism (PEP $\xrightarrow{k_6}$ Oxaloacetate $\xrightarrow{k_{19}}\dashv$ Malonyl-CoA) that induces homeostatic buffering and fundamentally breaks linear proportionality.

Given that Choice H ($[F] \ \neg\!\propto [B]$) directly accommodates the breakdown of proportionality induced by dominant negative feedback, while G relies on treating the network as an open-loop cascade, H remains the more rigorous and intended solution.
}

